WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.167
-Today is Friday. That's usually

00:00:02.167 --> 00:00:03.767
when I catch up
on some personal stuff.

00:00:03.767 --> 00:00:06.200
I check my inbox and return
some emails and, of course,

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:08.334
I send out thank-you notes.

00:00:08.334 --> 00:00:10.601
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:10.601 --> 00:00:13.000
-Wow.
-I was running
a bit behind today.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:14.801
-Today?
-Today. I was very busy.

00:00:14.801 --> 00:00:16.367
-What are you doing?
-Today?

00:00:16.367 --> 00:00:17.634
-Yeah.
-Oh, man.

00:00:17.634 --> 00:00:19.567
Well, I went to the skate park.

00:00:19.567 --> 00:00:21.467
[ Laughter ]
-Of course. Well,
that's usually every Friday.

00:00:21.467 --> 00:00:23.334
-Yeah, every Friday. Because
I'm working on some new tricks.

00:00:23.334 --> 00:00:24.534
-Yeah.
What do you got going?

00:00:24.534 --> 00:00:28.167
-I got like a 180 French roll.

00:00:28.167 --> 00:00:30.167
-Oh, a French roll? Oh.
-Yeah, I'm working on that.

00:00:30.167 --> 00:00:31.367
-Yeah?
-It's pretty cool, yeah.

00:00:31.367 --> 00:00:33.234
Kickflip type of jam.
-Yeah.

00:00:33.234 --> 00:00:34.567
-Jam.
-Yeah.

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:36.300
-I say "jahm" because that's --
-Oh, you say "jahm"

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:37.834
because you're cool, right?
[ Laughter ]

00:00:37.834 --> 00:00:39.100
-Well, I am cool, yeah,
but, also,

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:41.567
I learned to skate in Europe.
-Really? Where at?

00:00:41.567 --> 00:00:43.267
[ Laughter ]
-And that's how we say jam.

00:00:43.267 --> 00:00:45.767
-You just say "jahm"?
-"Jahm." What's your "jahm"?

00:00:45.767 --> 00:00:46.968
-Really?!
-Yeah, and it's cool, but,

00:00:46.968 --> 00:00:48.634
anyway, so I did that
and then I got, you know,

00:00:48.634 --> 00:00:50.367
a matching tattoo.

00:00:50.367 --> 00:00:51.501
-What'd you -- Who --

00:00:51.501 --> 00:00:53.067
You got a matching tattoo?
-Of your --

00:00:53.067 --> 00:00:54.601
-Of me?
-No, of your matching tattoo.

00:00:54.601 --> 00:00:55.834
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, oh, right.

00:00:55.834 --> 00:00:58.400
The one that says,
"I love lasagna."

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:00.234
[ Laughter ]
It's Garfield.
-No, I didn't get that one.

00:01:00.234 --> 00:01:01.801
I got the other one.
-Did you get the one

00:01:01.801 --> 00:01:03.501
that said --

00:01:03.501 --> 00:01:05.634
[ Laughter ]

00:01:05.634 --> 00:01:08.300
-No, no, no. That was more --
-Not the racy one?

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:11.267
-No, I got your back tattoo.
-Oh, oh, oh, of course.

00:01:11.267 --> 00:01:12.901
-Yeah. Spuds MacKenzie.

00:01:12.901 --> 00:01:14.534
-Yeah.
-And underneath that, it says,

00:01:14.534 --> 00:01:16.067
"Party animal,"
but spelled wrong.

00:01:16.067 --> 00:01:17.934
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.934 --> 00:01:20.567
No, I got "Pug life"
on the front of my --

00:01:20.567 --> 00:01:22.400
-Oh, nice.
With a little baby pug

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:23.968
and your bellybutton's
his butthole.

00:01:23.968 --> 00:01:24.868
-Yeah.
-That's so cute.

00:01:24.868 --> 00:01:26.601
[ Laughter ]
-Mouth, mouth.

00:01:26.601 --> 00:01:28.100
-Mouth.
I'm sorry, mouth.

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:31.033
-Guys, can I write out my weekly
thank-you notes right now?

00:01:31.033 --> 00:01:31.968
Is that cool?
James, can I get --

00:01:31.968 --> 00:01:34.267
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:01:34.267 --> 00:01:36.868
James, can I get some thank-you
note writing music, please?

00:01:36.868 --> 00:01:38.634
-[ Playing tender tune ]

00:01:38.634 --> 00:01:39.734
-He's always in a good mood.

00:01:39.734 --> 00:01:41.067
-Summertime James.
-Yeah.

00:01:41.067 --> 00:01:42.234
-Wow.
-Summertime James.

00:01:42.234 --> 00:01:43.801
Takes his tie right off.
-Yeah.

00:01:43.801 --> 00:01:45.467
[ Laughter ]
-He's like, "It's Friday.

00:01:45.467 --> 00:01:47.167
It's Saturday somewhere,"
is what he says.

00:01:47.167 --> 00:01:50.767
-Every day is Saturday for him.
-Yeah. He doesn't care.

00:01:50.767 --> 00:01:52.033
♪♪
[ Laughter ]

00:01:52.033 --> 00:01:54.501
Thank you, SPF 15,

00:01:54.501 --> 00:01:56.634
for being the nonfat,
dairy-free oat milk

00:01:56.634 --> 00:01:57.934
of the sunscreen world.

00:01:57.934 --> 00:01:59.868
[ Laughter and applause ]
-Doesn't really do anything.

00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:02.467
It's fine.
-Yeah.

00:02:04.067 --> 00:02:05.300
[ Laughs ]

00:02:05.300 --> 00:02:06.434
♪♪
[ Laughter ]

00:02:06.434 --> 00:02:09.601
-Thank you,
Wendy's new Strawberry Frosty...

00:02:09.601 --> 00:02:11.400
[ Laughter ]
for showing us what it
would look like

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:14.400
if Jimmy Neutron dyed his hair
pink and hid inside a cup.

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:16.701
[ Laughter, cheering,
and applause ]

00:02:17.267 --> 00:02:18.133
-[ As Neutron ]
Where am I?

00:02:22.501 --> 00:02:23.634
♪♪
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.634 --> 00:02:24.734
What?
-I'm just thinking about who I'm

00:02:24.734 --> 00:02:26.000
going to write
this thank-you note to.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:27.167
-Who are you going
to write it to? Because you're

00:02:27.167 --> 00:02:28.701
making them up as you go.
-That's correct.

00:02:28.701 --> 00:02:30.400
-Because you live in a state
of gratitude, yeah.

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:32.200
-Yeah, they're not pre-written.
-No, not at all.

00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:34.033
-And I'm not reading them
from here.
-No!

00:02:34.033 --> 00:02:36.501
[ Laughter ]
-I'm writing them right now
-From your heart.

00:02:36.501 --> 00:02:38.567
-and sending them out.
-Right. You mail them to people.

00:02:38.567 --> 00:02:40.534
-That's correct.
Using the U.S. Postal Service.

00:02:40.534 --> 00:02:42.133
-Yes. Yes.
-Here we go.

00:02:42.133 --> 00:02:43.434
-Who's this one to?

00:02:45.167 --> 00:02:46.667
♪♪
Oh.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.667 --> 00:02:48.801
-Thank you, Cornhole...

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:50.133
[ Laughter ]
-Okay.

00:02:50.133 --> 00:02:52.200
-...for being a game
that sounds dirty,

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:54.801
but is really just
a good old-fashioned game

00:02:54.801 --> 00:02:57.234
of tossing sacks
and penetrating holes.

00:02:57.234 --> 00:03:01.367
[ Laughter, cheering,
applause, and hooting ]

00:03:01.367 --> 00:03:02.067
-Wow!

00:03:04.067 --> 00:03:06.701
Costs you extra if you lick it.
There you go, yeah.

00:03:06.701 --> 00:03:08.167
[ Laughter ]

00:03:08.167 --> 00:03:10.300
Cornhole.
-That's correct.

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:11.934
-Yeah.
So is that to the makers

00:03:11.934 --> 00:03:12.734
of Cornhole?
-What's that?

00:03:12.734 --> 00:03:13.734
[ Laughter ]

00:03:13.734 --> 00:03:14.801
Could be the maker
of the Cornhole.

00:03:14.801 --> 00:03:17.434
Could be to the players
of Cornhole.

00:03:17.434 --> 00:03:19.267
It's like letters to Santa.
-So, when you put it
in the mail,

00:03:19.267 --> 00:03:20.968
does it just say Cornhole
and that's it

00:03:20.968 --> 00:03:22.467
and you throw it in there?
[ Laughter ]

00:03:22.467 --> 00:03:25.267
-No, it goes label-less
and just finds its way.

00:03:25.267 --> 00:03:26.501
-Like letters to Santa.
-Like letters to Santa,

00:03:26.501 --> 00:03:27.968
almost, yeah, yeah.
-Beautiful.

00:03:27.968 --> 00:03:29.367
-You got a good heart,
Jimmy Fallon.

00:03:29.367 --> 00:03:31.434
-What's that?
-You got a good heart.

00:03:31.434 --> 00:03:33.834
-I got a --
I got a good heart?

00:03:33.834 --> 00:03:36.767
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:36.767 --> 00:03:38.067
♪♪
[ Laughter ]

00:03:38.067 --> 00:03:40.400
-Thank you, leather jackets,

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:41.801
for making people look cool,

00:03:41.801 --> 00:03:43.868
smell like a shoe,
and sound like a couch.

00:03:43.868 --> 00:03:46.400
[ Laughter, cheering,
and applause ]

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:54.300
-[ Creaking ]

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:56.734
[ Laughter ]

00:03:56.734 --> 00:03:59.067
[ Creak ]
Thank you, weed whackers...

00:03:59.067 --> 00:04:00.801
-Oh!
-...for sounding like

00:04:00.801 --> 00:04:02.834
an old-school
anti-drug organization.

00:04:02.834 --> 00:04:03.801
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:03.801 --> 00:04:04.567
"No."

00:04:06.267 --> 00:04:08.734
-Just say no.
-Just say no.

00:04:08.734 --> 00:04:10.634
-Whack that weed!
-And whack that weed
out of their hand,

00:04:10.634 --> 00:04:12.133
is somebody offers it to you.
-Cornhole it!

00:04:12.133 --> 00:04:15.300
[ Laughter ]

00:04:15.300 --> 00:04:17.467
♪♪

00:04:17.467 --> 00:04:18.667
-Cornhole it!

00:04:18.667 --> 00:04:20.300
[ Laughter ]

00:04:20.300 --> 00:04:21.834
-That's what they yell
at the tournament.

00:04:21.834 --> 00:04:23.133
-Yeah, the tournament
before they start the game.

00:04:23.133 --> 00:04:25.400
-Yeah.
Everyone gets in there, ready.

00:04:25.400 --> 00:04:26.400
Cornhole it!
-Yep.

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:27.667
[ Laughter ]

00:04:27.667 --> 00:04:28.901
♪♪

00:04:28.901 --> 00:04:32.634
Thank you, the new Disney+
series "Obi-Wan Kenobi,"

00:04:32.634 --> 00:04:34.734
for being a sequel
to the prequels,

00:04:34.734 --> 00:04:36.267
but a prequel to the sequels.

00:04:36.267 --> 00:04:37.534
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:37.534 --> 00:04:39.367
We don't know, yet,
if we're getting a sequel

00:04:39.367 --> 00:04:42.100
to this prequel sequel
that's set before the requels,

00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:44.400
but, if I spend any more time
thinking about this,

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:45.868
I'm going to need some ZzzQuil.

00:04:45.868 --> 00:04:46.968
-No.

00:04:46.968 --> 00:04:48.801
[ Laughter, cheering,
and applause ]

00:04:49.567 --> 00:04:51.167
-[ Clucking ]

00:04:51.167 --> 00:04:51.934
[ Creaking ]

00:04:54.067 --> 00:04:58.100
[ Creaking ]

00:04:58.100 --> 00:04:58.767
Pbbt!

00:04:58.767 --> 00:05:00.200
[ Laughter ]

00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:02.033
[ Pop! ]

00:05:02.033 --> 00:05:02.701
Sss!

00:05:05.133 --> 00:05:08.000
[ Quacking ]

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:08.667
[ Laughter ]

00:05:08.667 --> 00:05:09.934
